# Environment Configuration Example
# Copy this file to .env and update with your values

# ============================================
# API CONFIGURATION
# ============================================

# Development API URL (your computer's local IP or ngrok URL)
# Example: http://192.168.1.100:3000
# Or ngrok: https://abc123.ngrok.io
API_URL_DEV=http://localhost:3000

# Production API URL (your deployed Next.js app)
# Example: https://your-app.vercel.app
API_URL_PROD=https://your-production-url.com

# ============================================
# FIREBASE CONFIGURATION
# ============================================
# Already configured in firebase/firebase-config.ts
# Uses the same Firebase project as the web app

# ============================================
# OPTIONAL: CUSTOM API KEY
# ============================================
# If you want users to provide their own Gemini API key
# This is already handled in the aiService
# GEMINI_API_KEY=your-api-key-here

# ============================================
# NOTES
# ============================================
# 1. For local development, use your computer's IP address
#    Find it with: ipconfig (Windows) or ifconfig (Mac/Linux)
#
# 2. Both phone and computer must be on the same WiFi network
#
# 3. Or use ngrok for easier testing:
#    ngrok http 3000
#    Then use the https URL from ngrok
#
# 4. For production, deploy your Next.js app and use that URL
